== FINDINGS (observations for the lead's backlog, not criterion failures) ==
F1 (relates to A2 / design point d): NO test in the repo -- worker's or oracle's
   -- discriminates the >=2 shared-token rule from >=1. Mutation M4 (`>= 2` ->
   `>= 1`) leaves the worker's nine new tests, the oracle's three tests and the
   full dataloader suite ALL GREEN. Root cause: the fixture behind both the
   oracle's `gapB-single-token` guard and the worker's
   TestDetect_ScheduledSettled_SingleSharedTokenNoMatch is "Monroe County Water
   Authority" vs "Wire Fee", which shares ZERO tokens, not one. The worker's own
   failure message is honest about this ("expected 0 pairs (0 shared tokens)");
   only the test NAME (inherited from the spec's A2 label "single-shared-token")
   overclaims. Not a FAIL: A1-A5 as written are met, the spec's own calibration
   text specifies the zero-token Wire Fee case, and I proved the >=2 boundary is
   behaviourally correct with a probe. Recommend the V3 pattern -- promote my
   throwaway probe into a committed test in near_duplicates_test.go using the
   spec's Lucid calibration (scheduled "Lucid" / posted "Lucid Bill Payment",
   same account, <=7 days => 0 pairs), which fails under M4 and passes today.
F2 (relates to design point c): the checkPrefixRE exclusion is implemented and
   load-bearing, but no committed test covers it -- M6 removes it with every
   test still green, because classify() claims the Hyundi regression fixture
   before Gap B is reached. A test needs a check-shaped Description that
   classify() does NOT claim (check desc + scheduled status), e.g. the probe pair
   I used. Same V3 follow-up.
F3 (informational): the `dayDiff(a.Date, b.Date) > duplicateWindowDays` guard
   inside isScheduledSettledPair (near_duplicates.go:284) is dead code relative
   to the caller -- detectNearDuplicatePairs:130 already rejects any diff >
   duplicateWindowDays. Harmless and spec-mandated; noting only so a future
   reader does not mistake M7's survival for a weak test.
